{% from "partials/source-icon.njk" import sourceIcon %}
{% from "partials/panel-icon.njk" import panelIcon %}
{% from "partials/mark.njk" import mark %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="oled" data-theme-mode="oled">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{% block title %}{{ title or 'Sign in' }}{% endblock %} · ModWatch</title>
  <meta name="description" content="ModWatch tracks Minecraft mods across modpacks and reports updates for the exact Minecraft version and loader you run.">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#000000">
  <link rel="icon" href="/assets/img/favicon.ico?v={{ assetVersion }}" sizes="any">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/assets/img/favicon.svg?v={{ assetVersion }}">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/assets/img/favicon-32.png?v={{ assetVersion }}">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/assets/img/favicon-16.png?v={{ assetVersion }}">
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/img/apple-touch-icon.png?v={{ assetVersion }}">
  <link rel="manifest" href="/assets/site.webmanifest?v={{ assetVersion }}">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="ModWatch">
  <meta property="og:title" content="Sign in · ModWatch">
  <meta property="og:description" content="Self-hosted Minecraft modpack update tracker for Forge, Fabric, NeoForge and Quilt.">
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ baseUrl }}/login">
  <meta property="og:image" content="{{ baseUrl }}/assets/img/og-image.png">
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  <script src="/assets/js/theme.js?v={{ assetVersion }}"></script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/modwatch.css?v={{ assetVersion }}">
</head>
<body class="auth-body" data-page="{{ page or 'login' }}">
<div class="auth">
  <section class="auth-brand" aria-label="About ModWatch">
    <a class="brand auth-wordmark" href="/login" aria-label="ModWatch">
      <img class="brand-mark" src="/assets/img/logo.svg?v={{ assetVersion }}" alt="" width="28" height="28">
      <span class="brand-name">ModWatch</span>
    </a>
    <div class="auth-copy">
      <h1>Know what is out of date before the pack starts.</h1>
        <p>ModWatch reads the mods inside a Minecraft modpack and checks each one against the exact Minecraft version and loader that pack runs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="auth-scope">
      <span class="scope-label">Supported sources</span>
      <div class="auth-support-list">
        <div class="auth-support-row">
          <div class="auth-support-copy">
            <span class="source-label modrinth">{{ sourceIcon('modrinth') }}Modrinth</span>
            {# <small>Search, hash lookup and version checks</small> #}
          </div>
          <span class="pill pos"><span class="dot"></span>Supported</span>
        </div>
        <div class="auth-support-row">
          <div class="auth-support-copy">
            <span class="source-label github">{{ sourceIcon('github') }}GitHub</span>
            {# <small>{% if env.githubReady %}Token connected · release checks{% else %}Public API · release checks{% endif %}</small> #}
          </div>
          <span class="pill pos"><span class="dot"></span>Supported</span>
        </div>
        <div class="auth-support-row">
          <div class="auth-support-copy">
            <span class="source-label curseforge">{{ sourceIcon('curseforge') }}CurseForge</span>
            {# <small>{% if env.curseforgeReady %}Official API connected · search and files{% else %}URL resolver ready · search key pending{% endif %}</small> #}
          </div>
          {% if env.curseforgeReady %}
          <span class="pill pos"><span class="dot"></span>Supported</span>
          {% else %}
          <span class="pill warn"><span class="dot"></span>Partial</span>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>The three connectors share one scope. CurseForge project URLs work without a key; search turns on when the API key is connected.</p>
      <span class="scope-label" style="margin-top: 10px;">Supported panel sync</span>
      <div class="auth-support-list">
        <div class="auth-support-row">
          <div class="auth-support-copy">
            <span class="source-label amp">{{ panelIcon('amp') }}CubeCoders AMP</span>
          </div>
          <span class="pill pos"><span class="dot"></span>Supported</span>
        </div>
        <div class="auth-support-row">
          <div class="auth-support-copy">
            <span class="source-label pterodactyl">{{ panelIcon('pterodactyl') }}Pterodactyl</span>
          </div>
          <span class="pill pos"><span class="dot"></span>Supported</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>Panel sync needs an account that can start and stop the server and read its files. ModWatch writes inside <code>mods/</code>, backs up first, and rolls back if the server does not come up.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="auth-foot">Self-hosted · v{{ appVersion }}</p>
  </section>
  <section class="auth-panel">
    <a class="brand auth-mobile-brand" href="/login" aria-label="ModWatch">
      <img class="brand-mark" src="/assets/img/logo.svg?v={{ assetVersion }}" alt="" width="28" height="28">
      <span class="brand-name">ModWatch</span>
    </a>
    <div class="auth-theme" id="auth-theme"></div>
    <div class="auth-form-wrap">
      {% include "partials/flash.njk" %}
      {% block content %}{% endblock %}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
<script src="/assets/js/ui.js?v={{ assetVersion }}"></script>
</body>
</html>
